{{- /*
aerc compose template — zentoo/jmapsyncd send path.

Enabled by:
  [templates]
  new-message = new_message
  [compose]
  edit-headers = true

The `X-JMAP-Send-At` header below is the scheduling primitive.
Values accepted:
  send-now                         → deliver immediately (default; can also
                                     be omitted entirely with the same effect)
  ISO8601 timestamp with timezone  → schedule delivery
    e.g. 2026-08-05T09:00:00Z
    e.g. 2026-08-05T09:00:00-05:00
    e.g. 2026-08-05T09:00:00+02:00

`jmapqueue` reads and strips this header before submitting to JMAP.  The
JMAP server (Fastmail, Stalwart, Cyrus) holds scheduled messages until the
timestamp.  Sending happens in the same request as filing to Sent
(EmailSubmission `onSuccessUpdateEmail`) so there's no window where the
message exists as an unfiled Draft.

Listing / cancelling scheduled sends (works for both immediate and
scheduled — an in-flight scheduled message can be canceled up to the
send-at timestamp):
  jmapsyncd submissions list --state scheduled
  jmapsyncd submissions cancel <id>
*/ -}}
X-Mailer: aerc {{version}}
X-JMAP-Send-At: send-now

{{ with .Body -}}{{.}}{{- end }}
{{- with .Signature }}

{{.}}{{- end }}
